{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1490999-tracking-a-prey-for-vampires","id":1490999,"title":"Tracking a prey for Vampires","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Vampire: The Requiem"],"posts":[{"date":"2022-08-22T08:44:09-07:00","id":1490999,"title":"Tracking a prey for Vampires","content":"I'm aware about the werewolf's Tracking system, and I kinda like that but I'm not sure it's fair to apply it as is when vampires are tracking each other. Reason this doubt of mine has arisen is that werewolves are more behaving like wolves, sniffing air, etc. And that could also be applied for Kindred with acute sense or protean's feral senses, but what about others kindred where blood is not involved? How would you handle, mechanically, this request from your players?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7079-marcus","name":"Marcus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7079_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1119"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-08-22T09:33:19-07:00","id":1491002,"title":"","content":"They don't need blood to hear heartbeats, Vampires can hear heartbeats at three meters or yards per dot of blood potency (I would decide ahead of time to use either yards or meters exclusively. The difference is small between one meter or yard, but gets significantly bigger at two or three). <br /> <br /> Otherwise, without Auspex, they're stuck doing footwork, or maybe doxing.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3201-father-enoch","name":"Father Enoch","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3201_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"285"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-08-22T09:42:19-07:00","id":1491003,"title":"","content":"The book is not exactly clear about how tracking is supposed to work, it is written that vampires who tasted someone's blood can track them, I always interpreted it as something similar as blood sympathy, you roll to see if you can feel that they are around and from there you start tracking but that is my own intrepretation of it since it might just mean that they can sniff the air when the prey is close and that's it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27142-newb95","name":"Newb95","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"502"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-08-22T09:44:43-07:00","id":1491004,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Father Enoch</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1490999-tracking-a-prey-for-vampires?p=1491002#post1491002\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">They don't need blood to hear heartbeats, Vampires can hear heartbeats at three meters or yards per dot of blood potency (I would decide ahead of time to use either yards or meters exclusively. The difference is small between one meter or yard, but gets significantly bigger at two or three). <br /> <br /> Otherwise, without Auspex, they're stuck doing footwork, or maybe doxing.</div> </div> </div> </div>When tracking 3 or 30 meters doesn't really have any impact since we talk about kms. Heartbeats may come into picture when trying to spot someone hided in the same area, and anyway has no meaning against others kindred.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7079-marcus","name":"Marcus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7079_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1119"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-08-22T19:18:19-07:00","id":1491070,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Newb95</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1490999-tracking-a-prey-for-vampires?p=1491003#post1491003\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The book is not exactly clear about how tracking is supposed to work, it is written that vampires who tasted someone's blood can track them, I always interpreted it as something similar as blood sympathy, you roll to see if you can feel that they are around and from there you start tracking but that is my own intrepretation of it since it might just mean that they can sniff the air when the prey is close and that's it.</div> </div> </div> </div>The bonus for having tasted a human's blood is specifically for tracking by scent, yes. You're possibly thinking of werewolves, who can automatically sense the direction of the last living prey whose blood they tasted for a lunar month, which doesn't affect their own tracking subsystems except in terms of making it possible to roll in circumstances where there might otherwise be too much time and distance between them and their target.<br /> <br /> <br /> I think it's a reasonable conclusion that tracking without a dedicated subsystem is just a regular roll using the Perception pool (Wits + Composure or a relevant Skill, likely Survival or Investigation), as an instant or extended action.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-08-27T08:53:37-07:00","id":1491480,"title":"","content":"For what I've seen, the tracking system accounts when the tracker is an Uratha, or not, letting Uratha have their primal urge tracking bonus. I agree that the system is most likely designed for hunters with enhanced senses; however, there is a penalty for prey leaving weak trail. This penalty could easily by applied for hunters that lack this senses. Vampires that do not posses acute senses, Protean 2, activate Auspex, etc., could experience the penalty on top. I believe hunting living prey should provide a -1 to -2 penalty as vampires have their senses attuned to hunt them. Tracking vampires on the other hand should be more difficult, a -3, as they don't bleed, sweat, have a heart beat and their beast unconsciously keeps them hidden as evidenced by the lost visage.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12173-basilistik","name":"Basilistik","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"33"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-08-27T10:20:16-07:00","id":1491491,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Basilistik</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1490999-tracking-a-prey-for-vampires?p=1491480#post1491480\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">For what I've seen, the tracking system accounts when the tracker is an Uratha, or not, letting Uratha have their primal urge tracking bonus. I agree that the system is most likely designed for hunters with enhanced senses; however, there is a penalty for prey leaving weak trail. This penalty could easily by applied for hunters that lack this senses. Vampires that do not posses acute senses, Protean 2, activate Auspex, etc., could experience the penalty on top. I believe hunting living prey should provide a -1 to -2 penalty as vampires have their senses attuned to hunt them. Tracking vampires on the other hand should be more difficult, a -3, as they don't bleed, sweat, have a heart beat and their beast unconsciously keeps them hidden as evidenced by the lost visage.</div> </div> </div> </div>Although mechanically that makes sense, how can It possibly be justified or described in-game where we have asphalt roads where footprints can be left and so many people are walking the very same streets? If we take out smell and blood I mean.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7079-marcus","name":"Marcus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7079_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1119"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-08-27T12:33:27-07:00","id":1491510,"title":"","content":"Tracking in the city is a very different action. If we eliminate scent (and supernatural senses) we are left with very little and must resort to a Sherlock Holmes style of tracking, basically an investigation. The sole of their shoes could have a very distinct print which they could follow, or their car a particular tire marks but that wont be enough. The Skill to track must be changed. Maybe Computers or Investigation to track their posts if they have online presence, some apps publish their location to their post if they have that information. You could go Socialize or Streetwise asking shops or street people if they have seen them. Some shops have cameras pointing out that the owners could let them you look if they come with a soap story like looking for their daughter, or daughter's killer or something applying Subterfuge. In my country, Taxi drivers are a powerful network the police and common people use to track people who stole cars or committed recent crimes. They could also use Persuasion to pay a gang to keep an eye out. I think in the city it'll be all about asking the right people.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12173-basilistik","name":"Basilistik","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"33"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}